doc.add_heading('Veer D0 High Level Design',0)
p('Course: Computer Science Senior Design I\nAdvisor: Dr. Jillian Aurisano\nTeam: Grady Algire, Brady Cooper, Briar Elliot, Dominic Rowland, Aiden Ward\nDesign version: 1.0 | October 2, 2026')
h('1. Title, goal statement, and conventions')
p('Project title: Veer. Goal: '+GOAL)
p('Veer is a mobile navigation service for a driver using a mounted phone. It interprets requests such as adding a food stop or avoiding rain, highways, or tolls as structured trip constraints, then proposes a revised route and provides turn-by-turn voice guidance.')
p('The basic inputs are driver speech, current phone location, destination, active trip constraints, and a local mute control. The basic outputs are a live route with spoken directions, a short spoken confirmation or recovery prompt, a visible listening/muted indicator, and per-trip API usage counts for the development team.')
p('Scope includes voice capture, transcription, constraint extraction, waypoint insertion by business or category, weather-aware route preferences, highway/toll preferences, and live guidance on the driver\'s phone. Raw audio is transient; no audio files are retained. Active constraints expire at trip end. Saved-trip accounts and a web trip planner are outside this first-release design.')
p('Conventions: C labels a component built by the team; E labels an external dependency. Solid blue boxes represent team components; dashed gray boxes represent dependencies or external actors. A block-diagram arrow initiates the interface; its response returns along that interface. A data-flow arrow names the information crossing it and its form. Each diagram includes this legend and the project goal.')
table(['Story','Capability','Responsible components'],[['US-01','Add a food stop with a detour no greater than 10 minutes.','C1, C2, C3'],['US-02','Use an avoid-rain constraint when selecting a route.','C1, C2, C3'],['US-03','Inspect AI and Maps call counts for each trip.','C2, C3, C4'],['US-04','Show listening state; stop capture with tap or voice mute.','C1'],['US-05','Confirm interpreted speech before changing a route.','C1, C2, C3']],[.6,4.8,1.8])
p('The supplied project description, stories, use cases, and clarified acceptance criteria govern this design. Explicit spoken approval is required; silence leaves the route unchanged. The route update must complete within 3 seconds after the driver finishes saying "okay." Section 7 records this decision and remaining D1 choices.')
page();h('2. Block diagram (the D0 diagram)');doc.add_picture(str(P/'D0_Block_Diagram.png'),width=Inches(7.15))
p('C1 runs on the phone; C2, C3, and C4 are logical modules within a shared backend. E1 is the existing phone platform, not hardware the team builds. E2 supplies transcription and constraint parsing; E3 supplies Google Maps routes and places; E4 supplies weather observations/forecasts. The developer is an external actor using I9. Drivers and passengers interact with C1 through the phone; these local interactions are detailed in I1.')
p('C1 owns active navigation state and the final route update. C2 returns a proposed constraint, not an instruction to mutate the route. C3 returns a route proposal after applying validated constraints. C4 stores consumption metadata only; it is not a repository for conversations, coordinates, or raw audio. Routing, weather integration, and mute implementation algorithms remain for D1/D2.')
page();h('3. Component responsibility table')
p('The table assigns primary responsibility for each component. Dominic Rowland owns the E4 weather integration task within C3; Brady Cooper owns C3 as a whole.')
table(['Component','One-sentence responsibility','Interfaces in / out','Primary owner'],[['C1 Mobile Navigation','Manage the driver\'s live navigation interaction.','In: I2/I4 replies, I1 device events; out: I1, I2, I4','Grady Algire'],['C2 Speech Understanding','Translate transient speech into proposed routing constraints.','In: I2; out: I3, I7','Briar Elliot'],['C3 Route Planning','Produce route proposals that satisfy validated trip constraints.','In: I4; out: I5, I6, I8','Brady Cooper'],['C4 Usage Monitor','Account for provider consumption by trip.','In: I7, I8, I9; out: I9 reply','Aiden Ward'],['E1 Phone Platform','Supply device input and output capabilities.','In: I1 control; out: I1 events','External; liaison Grady Algire'],['E2 AI Provider','Provide speech transcription and structured interpretation.','In: I3; out: I3 reply','External; liaison Briar Elliot'],['E3 Google Maps Platform','Supply route and place data.','In: I5; out: I5 reply','External; liaison Brady Cooper'],['E4 Weather Provider','Supply location-indexed precipitation information.','In: I6; out: I6 reply','External; integration owner Dominic Rowland']],[1.45,2.65,1.6,1.5])
p('Story coverage is shown in Section 1. Live guidance and highway/toll constraints additionally trace to the first-release scope in the project description.')
page();h('4. Interface specification table')
p('I3 uses secure WebSocket streaming (WSS), matching the speech-stream contract on I2. This permits a shared streaming design for utterance audio and interpretation replies; provider selection must support this proposed contract and the no-retention requirement. HTTPS batch uploads were considered but not selected for the continuous voice interaction.');
p('The following logical contracts define the D0 interfaces. Types: string = UTF-8; integer = whole number; number = finite decimal; boolean = true/false; instant = ISO 8601 UTC; [] = array; ? = optional; enum = one listed value. LatLng={lat:number, lon:number} in WGS84. Durations are seconds, distances are meters, precipitation probability is 0-1. JSON records use the named types defined after the table. Each network request includes requestId:string. Error={code:string, message:string, retryable:boolean}; a failure never silently applies a route.')
rows=[['I1 C1 <-> E1','In to E1: micControl:enum(start,stop,forceStop), locationControl:enum(start,stop), spokenText:string. Back to C1: audio:PCMFrame[], location:LocationFix, micState:enum(listening,muted,error), mute:MuteEvent, destination:LatLng?, acknowledgment:enum(accept,reject)?.','PCM bytes plus typed local events','Phone OS calls, callbacks, local UI events','C1 keeps indicator aligned with actual capture state. On mute it closes the send/capture gate, clears buffers, then stops mic; force-stop on failure. No post-request audio is sent or stored.'],['I2 C1 -> C2','Input: requestId:string, tripId:string, utteranceId:string, control:enum(audio,cancel), audio:binary?, audioMetadata:AudioMetadata. Output: transcript:string, intent:enum(propose,accept,reject,unknown), constraint:Constraint?, confidence:number, error:Error?.','Binary audio frames; JSON metadata/reply','Authenticated TLS stream (WSS)','C2 rejects invalid/unsupported audio and clears transient audio/transcript state on completion, cancel, or failure. C1 asks for repeat within 2 s after an unparseable utterance; route stays unchanged.'],['I3 C2 -> E2','Input: audio:binary, metadata:AudioMetadata, allowedConstraintTypes:string[], allowedIntents:string[]. Output: transcript:string, intent:enum(propose,accept,reject,unknown), constraint:Constraint?, confidence:number, usage:ProviderUsage.','Provider audio stream plus JSON','Authenticated TLS stream (WSS)','C2 handles timeout, quota, invalid output, or unclear speech. Validate structured output before forwarding. Zero-persistence provider behavior must be verified before selection; reject providers/configurations that retain raw audio.'],['I4 C1 -> C3','Input: requestId:string, tripId:string, location:LocationFix, destination:LatLng, currentRoute:RoutePlan?, constraints:Constraint[], tripRevision:integer. Output: proposal:RouteProposal?, error:Error?.','JSON','Authenticated HTTPS request/reply','C3 returns no_match, weather_unavailable, quota, or timeout explicitly. C1 keeps the active route and speaks a short recovery prompt. Ignore a stale tripRevision reply; require explicit spoken approval and finish route activation <= 3 s after "okay" ends. Silence cannot authorize an update.'],['I5 C3 -> E3','Input: origin:LatLng, destination:LatLng, waypoints:LatLng[], query:string?, avoidHighways:boolean, avoidTolls:boolean, alternatives:boolean. Output: routes:RoutePlan[], places:Place[], attribution:string.','Google provider JSON normalized to typed records','HTTPS request/reply','C3 handles no route/place match, quota, or timeout. Enforce detour <= 600 s for UC-01; otherwise unchanged route and alternate-place prompt <= 3 s. Do not claim Google accepts a weather-avoid flag.'],['I6 C3 -> E4','Input: samples:{location:LatLng, expectedAt:instant}[]. Output: weather:WeatherSample[], fetchedAt:instant.','Provider JSON normalized to typed records','HTTPS request/reply','C3 rejects stale/missing coverage for weather avoidance and reports that rain avoidance cannot be verified. Current guidance continues; no unsupported promise of a dry route.'],['I7 C2 -> C4','Input: event:UsageEvent for AI calls. Output: accepted:boolean, eventId:string.','Typed record','In-process call/return','C2 records an idempotent event for each outbound attempt, including retries; C4 deduplicates eventId. If unavailable, C2 keeps a metadata-only pending event and applies the configured quota policy.'],['I8 C3 -> C4','Input: event:UsageEvent for Maps/weather calls. Output: accepted:boolean, eventId:string.','Typed record','In-process call/return','C3 counts every outbound attempt, including failed calls and retries. C4 deduplicates. Unknown consumption triggers conservative budget handling; optional new replans may be denied while guidance continues.'],['I9 Developer -> C4','Input: developerAuth:string, tripId:string?, timeRange:{from:instant,to:instant}?. Output: summaries:UsageSummary[], error:Error?.','JSON','Developer-authenticated HTTPS GET','C4 denies unauthenticated/unauthorized access, rejects invalid filters, and labels incomplete totals. Return provider call counts without utterances, coordinates, or passenger information.']]
